  "body": "Found in a local run of the release tier (`cargo xtask gate release --no-snapshots`) on host uma.\n\nWhat happens: `crates/motion/tests/shape_masks.rs::shape_mask_catches_overcut_and_writes_diff_png` (added by PR #2098) writes its diff PNG under the fixed path `/tmp/shape-mask-unit-diffs/overcut/`. On uma that directory was already created by another user (`ghrunner`, the self-hosted runner account, mode 0775), so the test, run as `mikekinney`, fails:\n\n```\n(failed to write diff PNG: create png dir /tmp/shape-mask-unit-diffs/overcut: Permission denied (os error 13))\npanicked at crates/motion/tests/shape_masks.rs:229:48: expected diff png at \"/tmp/shape-mask-unit-diffs/overcut/overcut_unit.png\"\n```\n\nThe verdict part of the test is fine (108 overcut cells found as expected); only the fixed shared output path breaks it. Any machine where the runner user and a developer (or two worktrees in parallel) run the motion suites can turn the gate red for no code reason. This can hit the cut runner too.\n\nDone means: the test (and `crates/motion/tests/common/shape_mask.rs`) write diff PNGs under a per-run directory that no other user or run shares (for example `env!(\"CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR\")` or a fresh temp dir), and the test passes when `/tmp/shape-mask-unit-diffs` exists and belongs to another user.\n",
